    <bpmn:process id="W_W3732" name="W3732. Conflict of Interest &amp; Gifts/Integrity Disclosure Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Onboarding; annual cycle; new relationship/gift/event
Frequency: Annual + on event
Volume: Disclosures across at-risk roles
Owner: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Participants: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer, HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Procurement (links to VS-03/VS-34), Merchandising (links to VS-01), Finance (links to VS-17), ABC (links to VS-86.3), Legal (links to VS-100.3)
Source: workflow W3732 — Conflict of Interest &amp; Gifts/Integrity Disclosure Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3732_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3732_Lane1" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3732_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3732_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3732_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3732_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3732_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3732_Start3" name="Onboarding; annual cycle; new relationship/gift/event">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3732_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3732_Task4" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer operate the conflict-of-interest (COI) disclosure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer operate the conflict-of-interest (COI) disclosure program: annual COI declarations and on-change declarations for at-risk roles (procurement, merchandising, finance, B2G sales, AP, treasury), capturing outside interests, related-party relationships, and financial interests that could conflict with BuildRight
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / HR
Accountable (A): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Duration: Annual + on change</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3732_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3732_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3732_Task5" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer manage gifts &amp; entertainment (G&amp;E) per the G&amp;E…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer manage gifts &amp; entertainment (G&amp;E) per the G&amp;E policy (links to VS-86.3 anti-bribery): capture G&amp;E given/received above threshold, review for bribery/influence risk, approve/reject/declare, and maintain the G&amp;E register; integrate to ABC (links to VS-86.3)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / ABC / Function owners
Accountable (A): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Duration: On event + periodic</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3732_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3732_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3732_Task6" name="Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer review disclosed COIs/G&amp;E for actual/potential…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer review disclosed COIs/G&amp;E for actual/potential conflicts, manage recusal/mitigation, and report COI/G&amp;E posture and exceptions to the Ethics Committee (W3719) and audit (links to VS-21); refresh from case learning (W3728)
Responsible (R): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer / Audit
Accountable (A): Ethics &amp; Compliance Officer
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3732_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3732_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
